  clock: 2  # e76c
  nonce: e76c  # e76c
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES. The structural pair test is still call-graph reachability. The INV-duvup dependency is stale, and option (b) now collides with a ratified ADR clause.\n\n- taint.py:3797, in propagate_taint_structural (def at 3634): the test is still `if sink_node in reachable`. Two pair-level refusals were added in front of it after filing:\n  - _source_and_sink_are_one_call (INV-lozat, 95cc1521b4, 2026-08-31);\n  - _source_names_can_reach_sink (INV-fumod b, e66ab343a3, 2026-08-31), which is default-deny and only fires when both name sets are known (in practice the bash env/redirect names).\n  Neither is a value-flow check for the general case, so the row's FACT holds. collapsed_flow_count is still the collapse field (taint.py:690, 886).\n- Option (a) is NOT done: docs/measurements/README.md does not say what a row counts. Measurement 0012 (written after this row was filed) still publishes \"rows 30.0% / 28.8%\" beside situation with no reachability caveat (0012 line 18; README index row 64).\n- Option (b) collides with ADR-0048 F1 (docs/adr/0048 lines 66-70): \"The situation is canonical; the row rate is reported beside it every time, never instead\". Choosing (b) means amending a ratified frame clause through the owner, not just a docs change. (c) changes F1's row figure in the same way.\n- \"BLOCKS INV-duvup ... before the baseline series fixes its estimator\": INV-duvup was SATISFIED 2026-08-28 (PR #604, d181602ff7, ADR-0048 frame F1/F2/F8, gate scripts/check-measurement-frame, whose `unit` key exists). That is one day after this row was filed, and it fixed the estimator without addressing what a row counts. The ambiguity the row names is untouched; the dependency is not live.\n- The kamaraflow illustration (file-node source, count 8 against 1 os.makedirs site) was NOT re-measured.\n\nProposed item change: drop or rewrite the INV-duvup paragraph, and add ADR-0048 F1 as the clause that (b)/(c) would have to amend. The options' descriptions are otherwise still accurate."  # e76c
